### Cocos Challenge API - VS Code REST Client collection
### Install the "REST Client" extension, start the API (docker compose up) and click "Send Request".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@userId = 1
@pamp = 47

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Operational

### Liveness (no dependencies)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness (database ping)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Prometheus metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics

### OpenAPI document (Swagger UI at {{baseUrl}}/docs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs-json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Instruments

### Search by ticker fragment
GET {{api}}/instruments?q=pamp

### Search by name fragment (case-insensitive), 5 per page
GET {{api}}/instruments?q=banco&limit=5

### Explicit ticker + name filters (AND)
GET {{api}}/instruments?ticker=GGAL&name=galicia

### Full tradable list, page 2
GET {{api}}/instruments?page=2&limit=10

### One instrument with latest price and daily return
GET {{api}}/instruments/{{pamp}}

### Instrument without market data (prices are null)
GET {{api}}/instruments/3

### 404 problem+json
GET {{api}}/instruments/999

### 400 validation problem (limit > 100)
GET {{api}}/instruments?limit=500

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Portfolio

### Seed user 1: totalValue 904784.00, available cash 627500.00, PAMP + METR, warning for BMA
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/portfolio

### Empty portfolio
GET {{api}}/users/2/portfolio

### Unknown user -> 404 USER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{api}}/users/999/portfolio

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Orders

### MARKET BUY by exact size -> 201 FILLED at the last close
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 10 }

### MARKET BUY by ARS amount -> size = floor(amount / close) (100000 / 925.85 = 108)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "amount": "100000" }

### MARKET SELL -> 201 FILLED
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "SELL", "type": "MARKET", "size": 5 }

### LIMIT BUY -> 201 NEW (reserves cash until filled or cancelled)
# @name limitBuy
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "LIMIT", "size": 10, "price": "900.00" }

### Cancel the LIMIT order above -> 200 CANCELLED
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders/{{limitBuy.response.body.id}}/cancel

### LIMIT SELL -> 201 NEW (reserves shares)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "SELL", "type": "LIMIT", "size": 5, "price": "1000.00" }

### Insufficient cash -> 201 with status REJECTED / INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS (persisted)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 10000 }

### Insufficient shares -> 201 with status REJECTED / INSUFFICIENT_SHARES (persisted)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "SELL", "type": "MARKET", "size": 100000 }

### LIMIT without price -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "LIMIT", "size": 1 }

### MARKET with price -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1, "price": "900" }

### Both size and amount -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1, "amount": "1000" }

### Amount below one share -> 422 AMOUNT_TOO_SMALL (nothing persisted)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "amount": "900" }

### Cash instrument -> 422 NOT_TRADABLE
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": 66, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1 }

### Instrument without market data -> 422 NO_MARKET_PRICE
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": 3, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1 }

### Unknown instrument -> 404 INSTRUMENT_NOT_FOUND
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": 9999, "side": "BUY", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1 }

### Deposit cash -> 201 FILLED (side CASH_IN on ARS, price 1, size = amount)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/cash/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100000 }

### Withdraw cash within the available balance -> 201 FILLED (side CASH_OUT)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/cash/withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 50000 }

### Withdraw more than the available cash -> 201 REJECTED INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS (persisted)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/cash/withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999999 }

### Fractional amount -> 400 (whole ARS only)
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/cash/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10.5 }

### Cash sides are not accepted on the orders endpoint -> 400
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instrumentId": {{pamp}}, "side": "CASH_IN", "type": "MARKET", "size": 1000 }

### Cash movements in the history
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders?side=CASH_OUT

### Cancel a FILLED order -> 409 ORDER_NOT_CANCELLABLE
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders/2/cancel

### Cancel seed order 5 (NEW) -> 200 CANCELLED
POST {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders/5/cancel

### Order history, newest first (follow meta.nextCursor for the next page)
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders?limit=5

### Filter history
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders?status=NEW

### One order
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders/1

### Idempotent request id propagation (echoed in the response header and problem body)
GET {{api}}/users/{{userId}}/orders/999999
X-Request-Id: my-trace-id-123
